WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.413 --> 00:00:03.451
(birds chirping)

00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:06.595
(dog barks)

00:00:06.595 --> 00:00:09.178
(radio static)

00:00:10.153 --> 00:00:13.495
(sirens wailing)

00:00:13.495 --> 00:00:16.162
(intense music)

00:00:17.787 --> 00:00:20.470
(light music)

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.710
- Most people don't realize

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.923
that we're losing a
generation to violence.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.560
Kids in this area are in danger every day,

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.633
even going to school.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.350
I mean, literally thousands
are being shot every year.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.453
Hundreds dying from gun
violence, it's senseless.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.440
You can look in their
eyes and see hopelessness.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.283
They don't believe they're
gonna live to see 21, 25.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.003
So they don't plan for a future,

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.570
so violence is cool because in their mind

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.020
they're gonna be gone anyway.

00:01:02.506 --> 00:01:04.860
I realize they need
somebody in the community

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.513
besides the gang, that believes in them.

00:01:08.695 --> 00:01:11.195
(light music)

00:01:15.954 --> 00:01:18.704
(birds chirping)

00:01:23.744 --> 00:01:26.244
(dog barking)

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.340
My mom brought me into Chicago
when I was two weeks old,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.323
and we've been here ever since.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.340
Eight kids, 15 grandkids.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.243
I have my family all around me.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.510
15 years ago, my daughter Ayesha was 13.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:51.560
She had nine friends, girls and boys,

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.160
and I saw 'em running up and
down the street and I was like,

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.360
what they gonna do next?

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.980
They're young people, they need
stuff to keep them occupied.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.720
So when they're out in the community

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.800
and they're around the
kids that are in gangs,

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.500
well then they got the next thing.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.660
I knew they were at that stage,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.800
and I wanted to give them a safe place

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.710
away from all that, so I had an epiphany.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.282
I went out there and I
brought 'em into my house.

00:02:21.282 --> 00:02:23.088
Hey.
- Hey Miss Diane.

00:02:23.088 --> 00:02:25.171
- How you are now?
- Good.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.627
- They told me in those
first few hours, you know,

00:02:30.627 --> 00:02:32.760
"I'm failing in school, I need help."

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.620
Or, "My dad's gone and my mom's on drugs."

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.533
You know, I'm like, I'm in shock.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.370
From there I just
started getting involved.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.453
I start sitting with them and listening.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.670
In the next couple of days there were kids

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.020
started knocking on my
door that I didn't know,

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.050
and they were saying,
"Are you Miss Diane?"

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.260
And I'm like, "Yeah."

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.237
And they're like, "So and
so said you could help me."

00:02:56.237 --> 00:02:58.130
"I wanna go back to school."

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.010
And then the next day
there were five and six,

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.920
and then they were saying, "I
wanna get out of the gang."

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.504
Then homeless kids were
at my door late at night,

00:03:05.504 --> 00:03:08.130
and I honestly didn't
know what I was doing,

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.100
I just wanted to do it.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.560
You want to try another, find a job?

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.090
What you trying to do?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.940
- I feel I could get a job any time.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.730
- Well, why you haven't though?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.420
You 18 now, right?

00:03:20.503 --> 00:03:23.268
So, it's time.

00:03:23.268 --> 00:03:24.520
- It is time right now.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.570
- I was worried about
you there for a minute,

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.320
'cause there was too much going on.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:35.823
It seemed like you was angry
about it too, but you good now.

00:03:36.738 --> 00:03:37.929
Yeah.

00:03:37.929 --> 00:03:40.429
(light music)

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.200
This is 119th Street, one
of the most violent areas,

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.533
or I'd say the most violent
area in our community.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.280
At first it makes you want to run,

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.870
like nothing's gonna change.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.233
Just get out, just go do something else,

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.497
and then you go, no.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.670
If we leave, then what?

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:11.503
I mean,

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.553
I can't do everything, but
I can do what I can do.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.560
When you live on a block with 10 houses

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.150
and there's five or six
who have lost people

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:28.150
to gun violence, then it
affects the whole neighborhood,

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:33.048
and so I really wanted to help.

00:04:33.048 --> 00:04:35.890
(light instrumental music)

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:40.890
Kids Off the Block, KOB, is
an organization unto itself.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.670
During the school months,

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.430
we provide after school programming,

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.750
which consists of the tutoring,

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.973
and the mentoring and workshops.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:54.803
Then in the summer months,
violence heats up a lot.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.090
I saw a need, and there was a
vacant lot across the street,

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.423
so I turned it into a basketball court.

00:05:05.626 --> 00:05:07.747
Go play Mariano.

00:05:07.747 --> 00:05:10.659
Oh, he made it! (clapping)

00:05:10.659 --> 00:05:12.110
That's crazy.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:16.880
When the kids are playing
basketball, nothing else matters,

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.360
and that's just the truth.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.910
It's a powerful thing.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.830
It literally brings boys together

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.230
who are in different gangs,
who are in different cliques.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:28.190
They play on the court
together, or they eat together,

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.751
or they laugh together, so
that's what it's there for.

00:05:31.751 --> 00:05:35.100
(light instrumental music)

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.860
We estimated that over 3,000 young people

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.243
have been impacted or
come through the program.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.620
It became so many reasons

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.663
to come to KOB instead of the gang.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.603
So we became a force.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.538
- [Man] Three, two, one.

00:05:52.538 --> 00:05:53.618
Let's get involved here.

00:05:53.618 --> 00:05:56.285
(whistle blows)

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:01.640
- When I hear that someone's
been shot or killed,

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:02.593
it drains you.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.610
I wanted to do something that
would shock my community,

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.140
let the young people see

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.770
they're losing their friends to violence,

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.570
and that's how the memorial started.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.263
Those young people on those
stones, somebody loved them.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.920
They belonged to people,
they're not just names;

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:27.530
they were actually living
life, and they're gone.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:31.059
It makes you think how
fragile life is for all of us.

00:06:31.059 --> 00:06:35.070
(light instrumental music)

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:40.070
There are 791 stones, and we
still have 421 names there.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:45.400
Every one of them over
there is under 24 years old.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:51.220
I've seen two gang members
literally come to the memorial,

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.620
and go out and get a job,
and go back to school.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:54.453
(laughs)

00:06:54.453 --> 00:06:55.453
Seriously, the next day.

00:06:56.507 --> 00:07:01.507
(light instrumental music)
(birds chirping)

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:07.380
Today we're expanding.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:10.530
We actually have a space
next door in a building,

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.373
and we can get out of my house.

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:15.000
The space isn't ready yet,

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.630
but I know what it's gonna
look like, so I'm excited.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.433
Here will be our computer lab.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:26.063
Computers and printers, and desks.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.253
Here will be our music
studio right in the middle,

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.320
and over there on the side

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.173
will be our clothing design program.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.060
They need lifetime career skills,

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:42.933
and for us to able to give
them that will take the power,

00:07:42.933 --> 00:07:45.833
the violence, the guns,
the gangs, all of that out.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.303
- Miss Diane brought
peace to the neighborhood.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.890
I used to get like in
trouble all the time.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.690
I probably woulda like,
gotten into gangs and stuff,

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:59.460
but Miss Diane told me just to be myself.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:00.860
Be a leader, not a follower.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:04.240
- If it wasn't for Miss Diane,

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.290
I honestly wouldn't know where I'd be at,

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.230
'cause I've been through a lot.

00:08:10.493 --> 00:08:12.513
She always been there for me.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.300
- Be careful out here.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.490
- Miss Diane has done a
lot for this community.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:22.490
From feeding, to clothing,
to housing, to mentoring.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:26.569
Me, myself, I call her the
Big Mama of this generation.

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:29.758
- How you doing, Mama?
- How are you?

00:08:29.758 --> 00:08:33.880
- What you're doing makes a
difference in the community,

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.463
and each and every mother
who lost their child.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.230
- She doesn't back off and give in easy;

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:41.790
if she has an idea,

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.740
she'll stop at nothing to make it happen,

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.105
and that's what she does.

00:08:46.105 --> 00:08:49.277
(light instrumental music)

00:08:49.277 --> 00:08:50.534
- It was kinda rough around here

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:53.520
before she started Kids Off the Block.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:54.767
She always looking out.

00:08:59.312 --> 00:09:02.895
(light instrumental music)

00:09:04.359 --> 00:09:06.140
- [Diane] I don't think a
kid should have to be worried

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.903
that they can't walk their own street.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.753
A kid should be worried
about his bubblegum rapper.

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:19.123
A 17-year-old should be
worried about prom, graduating.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:26.380
African American youth are not the enemy,

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:28.497
and it's people like
myself who are out here,

00:09:28.497 --> 00:09:31.423
who are fighting every day
to change that perception,

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.770
and we're gonna do it.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:38.243
We might not have big money,
corporations and all that,

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.453
but never doubt people like us,

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.510
'cause we'll find a
way because we live it.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.190
Stop judging our young people.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.530
Give them the same opportunities
that everybody else gets,

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.343
'cause I guarantee you
you'll find some geniuses.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.960
Just give them the opportunity.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.250
My goal is for Kids Off the Block

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:06.190
to be in every city in this nation,

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.373
and we're working on that.

00:10:08.373 --> 00:10:10.690
(light instrumental music)

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:14.263
I've been doing this for 15
years, and I'm not stopping.

00:10:16.158 --> 00:10:19.741
(light instrumental music)

